   "text": {
    "L1": "Earth is called the blue planet because about 71 percent of its surface is water, while about 29 percent is land.",
    "L2": "So the belief that Earth has more land than water is not correct.",
    "L3": "There are seven continents: Asia, Africa, North America, South America, Antarctica, Europe and Australia.",
    "L4": "Asia is the largest continent, and Australia is the smallest.",
    "L5": "India is a country in Asia. The Indian Ocean is south of India, the Arabian Sea is west, and the Bay of Bengal is east.",
    "L6": "There are five oceans, and they are all connected rather than closed off from one another.",
    "L7": "From largest to smallest, the oceans are Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern and Arctic.",
    "L8": "Oceans give food and salt, affect weather and rainfall, and carry trade across sea routes."
   },
